# Cell from playpick: mode=menus, view=820x1180,touch, save=carried.
#
# The one prior menus/carried/820x1180 session (2026-09-25-9) covered the
# front page -> raid setup -> difficulty dropdown -> classpick -> compose ->
# an individual slot tap -> back x3 -> settings (viewed, not touched) ->
# record. What that session never touched: any of the three SHARE buttons
# (front page, daily, results) described in README.md's "Sharing" section,
# the settings screen's name field and volume stepper (viewed but not
# pressed), the DAILY screen's own layout (only ever visited mid-fight
# script, never surveyed with `ui`), and the BATTLEGROUND setup screen
# (map picker + composition), which has only ever been passed through on
# the way to a pull, never listed and measured on its own. This session
# does those four, short block at a time.

open
targets
ui
shot front

# The front page's own share is "about the game", no fragment -- README says
# it carries one line naming the record's furthest boss. Never pressed.
tap share
shot front-shared
note the front page's own SHARE button, first time this job has pressed it
targets

open
tap settings
targets
ui
shot settings

# Name field: README says an on-canvas field can't be typed into, so a real
# <input> is laid over the row. First time this job has focused it (no
# `type` verb in the driver vocabulary, so text entry itself is out of
# scope for a scripted session).
tap name
shot name-focused

# The camera row: never surveyed with `ui`, and README's own "How close the
# camera sits" section describes it as four settings with the closest as
# default -- worth checking the live control count against that claim.
targets

tap back
open
tap battleground
targets
ui
shot bg-setup

open
tap daily
targets
ui
shot daily-screen
